      "mergeID": "67571cf039cd76a4db99940f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I have been playing VR now for a little over a year and very recently with the new update I am experiencing issues,\n\nI jumped into VR chat two days ago and everything was fine, but today I have jumped into VR chat and I am experiencing some really annoying things, everything seems to be running pretty slow I'm experiencing frame drops, and my avatars I've had saved for a long time now are now looking less detailed and just lower textures, along with worlds I have been to very recently we're running absolutely fine are now on playable, plus all my settings on my profile were all reset and it's really annoying having to change everything back to the way it was, but the biggest issue is the compression problem, now I am not an expert in this kind of stuff so please bear with me. \n\nFirst off I should explain that I am only using the meta quest 2 standalone, in my settings when I last checked my compression was 500 megabytes and now I've noticed that it's been reduced to 40 megabytes which is making everything look terrible and unplayable, this is so unfair.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Compression with avatars and worlds problem",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6753f9d8c911b8761dce94e1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is due to vrchats new mipmap streaming they say it’s to help reduce crashes and being sent back to your home world but instead it causes random lag spikes and making a lot of avatars look like trash plus as an added bonus they made it to where it is enforced on quest and cannot be disabled but the thing is that quest barely crashed anymore and only crashed if it was internet issues \n\nSo the lower quality is technically not a bug even though it’s very annoying and personally I think shouldn’t be forced on by default on quest and should be either removed or let us toggle it off so we get that quality back",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
